    {
        "content": "<p>The docstring for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.star_mul#doc\">docs#Matrix.star_mul</a> caught my attention:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A version of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/ConjTranspose.html#Matrix.star_mul\"><code>star_mul</code></a> for <code>*</code> instead of <code>*</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I assume the comment used to have some meaning but became obsolete when we started spelling matrix multiplication with <code>HMul</code>. Shall we just remove the docstring altogether?</p>",
        "id": 587729541,
        "sender_full_name": "Anne Baanen",
        "timestamp": 1776680744
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is the lemma still needed?</p>",
        "id": 587730529,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776681061
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>there doesn't seem to be a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=star_mul#doc\">docs#star_mul</a> ! just <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=star_mul%27#doc\">docs#star_mul'</a></p>",
        "id": 587730694,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Rodriguez",
        "timestamp": 1776681122
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/6487\">#6487</a> changed the docstring (which lived in <code>Data/Matrix/Basic.lean</code> at the time) and the statement from</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- A version of `star_mul` for `⬝` instead of `*`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">star_mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NonUnitalSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">StarRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">star</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⬝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">star</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⬝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">star</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 587730941,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1776681204
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.star_mul#doc\">docs#Matrix.star_mul</a></p>",
        "id": 587731152,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1776681282
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the <code>star_mul</code> docstring is referring to is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=StarMul.star_mul#doc\">docs#StarMul.star_mul</a>, which gets exported to the root namespace (but doc-gen4 doesn't pick up on that).</p>",
        "id": 587731183,
        "sender_full_name": "Anne Baanen",
        "timestamp": 1776681290
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It turns out <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.star_mul#doc\">docs#Matrix.star_mul</a> was indeed slightly stronger than <code>star_mul</code>, except we can generalize a typeclass assumption and now they are exactly the same. I'll open a PR.</p>",
        "id": 587815164,
        "sender_full_name": "Anne Baanen",
        "timestamp": 1776703768
    }
]